# The Vercel project's Root Directory is ".", so a deploy uploads this whole
# repo, not just web/. Keep the workshop out of it.
#
# brand/ is ~25 MB of generated PNGs, reference images and vendored fonts. The
# Next app never imports from it and nothing in it is served, so it only ever
# cost upload and build time — but that is a cost for nothing on every deploy.
brand/

# anchor/target is 22,742 files of Rust build output and, on its own, pushed a
# deploy past Vercel's 15,000-file upload limit. The Next app imports nothing
# from anchor/ — the vault decoders in web/src/lib/vault are hand-written and
# do not read the IDL — so the whole Rust workspace stays out.
anchor/
backend/node_modules/
backend/data/
